            <p>Charles de Gaulle processed over 67 million passengers annually before pandemic disruptions, ranking as Europe's second-busiest airport and the primary hub for Air France's global network. Its role as the anchor of French aviation ensures that Seattle arrivals connect seamlessly to destinations across France, Europe, Africa, and beyond. </p>
            <h2>Airlines Flying from Seattle to Paris</h2>
            <p>A competitive field of carriers serves this corridor, with nonstop operations vying against connecting itineraries through North American and European hubs. </p>
            <h3>Full-Service Carriers</h3>
            <h4>Air France</h4>
            <p>As France's flag carrier and a founding SkyTeam member, Air France commands natural dominance on this route. </p>
            <h5>Signature elements: </h5>
            <ul>
                <li>Seasonal nonstop service from SEA to Paris CDG, typically operating May through October</li>
                <li>Boeing 787-9 Dreamliner and Airbus A330-200 deployment</li>
                <li>Evening departures arriving in Paris in the morning with a full day ahead</li>
                <li>La Première first class and Business class featuring lie-flat seats and French gastronomy</li>
                <li>Flying Blue loyalty program with extensive partner earning opportunities</li>
                <li>Strong domestic French network and European connections beyond Paris</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Delta Air Lines</h4>
            <p>Delta operates the primary year-round nonstop service and leverages its SkyTeam partnership with Air France. </p>
            <h5>Distinguishing characteristics: </h5>
            <ul>
                <li>Year-round nonstop service from SEA to Paris CDG, typically daily during peak season and 4-5 weekly in winter</li>
                <li>Airbus A330-900neo and Boeing 767-400ER equipment</li>
                <li>SkyMiles earning with Air France codeshare integration</li>
                <li>Delta One suites featuring lie-flat seats and Mediterranean-inspired dining</li>
                <li>Strong Seattle hub presence with extensive domestic feeder network</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Icelandair</h4>
            <p>Icelandair offers an intriguing alternative routing through its Reykjavik hub. </p>
            <h5>Competitive positioning: </h5>
            <ul>
                <li>Connections through Reykjavik (KEF) with competitive all-in pricing</li>
                <li>Free stopover program allowing multi-day Iceland visits at no extra cost</li>
                <li>Boeing 737 MAX and 757-200 equipment</li>
                <li>Saga Club loyalty program</li>
                <li>Often the most economical option for flexible travelers</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>British Airways</h4>
            <p>British Airways routes Seattle passengers through its London Heathrow hub. </p>
            <h5>Appeal: </h5>
            <ul>
                <li>Connections through London Heathrow (LHR) with multiple daily Seattle-London frequencies</li>
                <li>Convenient for UK-France combination trips</li>
                <li>Executive Club Avios earning</li>
                <li>Club World and First Class products</li>
                <li>Eurostar connection from London to Paris in 2 hours 15 minutes</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>United Airlines</h4>
            <p>United competes through its Chicago, Newark, and San Francisco hubs. </p>
            <h5>Notable features: </h5>
            <ul>
                <li>Connections through Chicago O'Hare (ORD), Newark (EWR), and San Francisco (SFO)</li>
                <li>MileagePlus earning with Lufthansa/Austrian/Swiss partnerships</li>
                <li>Polaris business class on long-haul segments</li>
                <li>Star Alliance connectivity for European beyonds</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Lufthansa / Austrian / Swiss</h4>
            <p>Star Alliance connections through Frankfurt, Munich, Vienna, or Zurich. </p>
            <h5>Value proposition: </h5>
            <ul>
                <li>Reliable European connections with short layovers</li>
                <li>Premium cabin consistency</li>
                <li>Strong network into secondary French destinations</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>KLM</h4>
            <p>SkyTeam alliance routing through Amsterdam. </p>
            <h5>Benefits: </h5>
            <ul>
                <li>Strong European connectivity</li>
                <li>Convenient for Netherlands-France combinations</li>
                <li>Flying Blue earning opportunities</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Virgin Atlantic</h4>
            <p>Virgin Atlantic offers an alternative British flavor through its Delta partnership. </p>
            <h5>Characteristics: </h5>
            <ul>
                <li>Connections through London Heathrow and Manchester</li>
                <li>Distinctive onboard service and entertainment</li>
                <li>Flying Club earning with Delta SkyMiles reciprocity</li>
                <li>Upper Class premium cabin with onboard bar</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Low-Cost and Hybrid Options</h3>
            <h4>Norse Atlantic Airways</h4>
            <p>Norwegian long-haul low-cost operator. </p>
            <h5>Positioning: </h5>
            <ul>
                <li>Connections through European points</li>
                <li>Ultra-low base fares</li>
                <li>Pay-for-what-you-need model</li>
            </ul>
