                <li>à la carte service additions</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Codeshare and Partnership Arrangements</h4>
            <p>Behind-the-scenes partnerships multiply apparent options: </p>
            <ul>
                <li>Air France and Delta coordinate extensively through SkyTeam and their transatlantic joint venture</li>
                <li>Delta and Virgin Atlantic maintain a revenue-sharing partnership</li>
                <li>United and Lufthansa/Austrian/Swiss connect through Star Alliance</li>
                <li>These arrangements protect passengers during irregular operations and simplify mileage earning</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Seasonal Variations</h3>
            <p>Pricing and availability shift markedly across the calendar, shaped by French tourism patterns, Pacific Northwest weather cycles, and American vacation habits. </p>
            <h4>Peak Season: June Through August</h4>
            <p>Summer transforms Paris into the world's most coveted European destination. </p>
            <h5>Market dynamics: </h5>
            <ul>
                <li>Economy round-trips climb to $1,100-$2,200</li>
                <li>Premium cabins reach $3,500-$6,500</li>
                <li>Delta nonstop operates at maximum frequency; Air France seasonal nonstop active</li>
                <li>Booking of 2-4 months essential for reasonable pricing</li>
                <li>Hotel inventory in central arrondissements compresses dramatically</li>
            </ul>
            <h5>Premium expense periods: </h5>
            <ul>
                <li><b>Late June through July</b> - European holiday commencement</li>
                <li><b>August</b> - Traditional French vacation month; some shops close, but major attractions remain packed</li>
                <li><b>Bastille Day week (July 14)</b> - National celebration drawing domestic and international visitors</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Shoulder Windows: April to May, September to October</h4>
            <p>These intervals reward flexible travelers with exceptional value and sublime conditions. </p>
            <h5>Why shoulders captivate: </h5>
            <ul>
                <li>Fares retreat 25-40% from summer peaks</li>
                <li>Temperatures ideal for walking the city's boulevards and gardens</li>
                <li>Crowds thin at the Louvre, Eiffel Tower, and Versailles</li>
                <li>Café terraces remain active without the summer crush</li>
                <li>Fashion Week events in September and October add cultural cachet</li>
                <li>Seattle's persistent spring drizzle makes Parisian sunshine particularly appealing</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Low Season: November Through March</h4>
            <p>Winter presents budget opportunities alongside distinctly Parisian atmospheric charm. </p>
            <h5>Financial advantages: </h5>
            <ul>
                <li>Economy tickets frequently available at $550-$950 round-trip</li>
                <li>Business class drops to $2,200-$3,800</li>
                <li>Christmas markets along the Champs-Élysées and at Notre-Dame create magical ambiance</li>
                <li>January sales (soldes) attract fashion-conscious shoppers</li>
                <li>Museum queues virtually disappear</li>
            </ul>
            <h5>Seasonal compromises: </h5>
            <ul>
                <li>Shortened daylight hours restrict outdoor sightseeing</li>
                <li>January and February bring chill and occasional gray drizzle</li>
                <li>Some river cruise and tour operations reduce frequency</li>
                <li>Restaurant terraces shutter, though heated outdoor seating persists</li>
            </ul>
            <h5>Calendar Events Affecting Costs: </h5>
            <ul>
                <li><b>Paris Fashion Week</b> (February/March and September/October) - Hotel compression and premium airfares</li>
                <li><b>French Open</b> (Roland Garros, late May-early June) - Tennis-driven demand spike</li>
                <li><b>Bastille Day</b> (July 14) - National holiday with fireworks and celebrations</li>
                <li><b>Christmas and New Year</b> - Premium pricing with strong booking requirements</li>
                <li><b>Valentine's Day</b> - Brief romance-driven demand increase</li>
            </ul>
